to the ingestion of food and costs coupled to the growth of body tissue. Whereas
DEB assumes that all these costs depend in a different way on body size (e.g.
maintenance costs relate to body structural volume, whereas heating costs relate
to surface area), IBP-type studies usually apply allometric curve fitting to
