4.6. Temperature and growth
DEB theory assumes that for a particular species, all rates (e.g. ingestion
rate, respiration rate, growth rate) can be described, within a species-specific
tolerance range, by an Arrhenius relationship using a single Arrhenius
temperature. The rationale behind this assumption is that if different processes
were governed by a different Arrhenius temperature, animals would face an
almost impossible task of coordinating the various processes. Van Haren and


